n: Therefore, Xiao Zheng is the driver.\n   - This does not follow the same modus ponens structure because the conclusion is not necessarily true based on the premises. It is a form of affirming the consequent, which is not the same as modus ponens.\n\nD) **A good doctor needs superb medical skills and noble medical ethics. xiao chen has both, so he is a good doctor**\n   - Premise 1: A good doctor needs superb medical skills and noble medical ethics.\n   - Premise 2: Xiao Chen has both superb medical skills and noble medical ethics.\n   - Conclusion: Therefore, Xiao Chen is a good doctor.\n   - This follows the same modus ponens structure as the original context.\n\nBased on the analysis, options A and D both follow the same modus ponens structure as the original context. However, option A is more directly similar to the dealer's logic because it involves a specific instance (xiao li) rather than a general rule (all drivers). Therefore, the most similar option is:\n\n<answer>A) The students in class 3 are diligent and studious. xiao li is a student in class 3, so xiao li is diligent and studious</answer>",
